Trump versus the establishment i'm jason  chaffetz in tonight for Shawn just 24  hours ago many in the mainstream media  were openly mocking President Trump for  losses in the stock market and  ridiculing him for not visiting our  troops during the Christmas season once  again the destroyed Trump press looks a  bit foolish today the stock market  bounced back with a record single day  point gain and president Trump along  with the first lady Melania Trump spent  the day with our troops after a surprise  visit to a rock where he shared his  gratitude for all of America's brave  servicemen and women watch this thank  you and every service member throughout  this region for the near elimination of  the ISIS territorial Caliphate in Iraq  and in Syria two years ago when I became  president they were a very dominant  group they were very dominant today  they're not so dominant anymore  on his way back from Iraq president  Trump visited US soldiers in Germany  we'll keep you updated on his surprise  trip throughout the show but first  joining us now with reaction the author  of why we fight Fox News national  security strategist Sebastian Gorka  former press secretary for vice  president prince and member of the Trump  2020 advisory board Marc Lauder and from  The Wall Street Journal one of my  personal favorites Kimberly Straus all  thank you all three of you for joining  us on this beautiful night in this great  holiday season I want to start with dr.  Gorka here the president is out there I  think one of the great strengths of the  president has been his foreign policy  but there have been some moves what's  the signal and the message that the  president is trying to portray out there  to the world well Merry Christmas Jason  it's a very simple one it is the  antithesis of the previous eight years  under the Obama White House remember  under that administration we had  concepts such as leading from behind  which is of course in oxymoron and  strategic patience allowing others to  take the initiative built into the  foreign policy of the United States  basically America withdrew from the  world and allow  others like Putin like Isis like China  like Iran to take the initiative and  destabilize the globe what you saw today  I spoke with the White House yesterday  as a president when his was on his way  to Iraq what you see is an expression of  American leadership reasserted whether  it's saying in Syria look we've done  what we came to do the Caliphate is  destroyed now others have to pick up the  load or whether it is spending your  Christmas as commander-in-chief with the  first lady the first time ever the first  lady in my understanding has visited  Iraq since 9/11 taking your Christmas  celebration and taking it to the Troops  and that amazing moment that Sarah  Huckabee Saunders shared with us when  one of our servicemen said to the  president I came back into the armed  services because of You mr. president  and his response was what I am here now  in Iraq because of you that's the make  America great again way and that's  Donald Trump now mark what does it tell  us about the perspective from the  international community we are the  world's pre-eminent superpower so what  is the message of President Trump is  putting out there by being on the ground  himself in Iraq I think if it's a strong  message that the president has our ala  has on the backs of our soldiers and our  airmen and our sailors no matter where  they're stationed in the world and he  showed that he demonstrated that and  this is a president who's also stood  with them by rebuilding our military and  so much emphasis has been placed today  on the launch of the hypersonic missile  over in in Russia this is a president  now who saw our military decimated under  the Obama administration  he stood up he's rebuilding our military  he is putting us in a position where we  can defend ourselves and our allies  around the world and our enemies know it  at Kim there's been a lot of discussion  certainly over the last week with the  moves in Syria and whatnot but is it  this also about Iran I mean the  proximity cannot get lost we hear almost  nothing being mentioned about Iran and  the message that this might send to the  Iranians and the Europeans and others  about our positioning on Iran how do  read into that well that's why this was  so important because coming on the back  of the announcements about Syria and  Afghanistan the worry was of course at  the message it was being sent to Iran  was that we were not certain about our  commitment in key areas in that region  and by going there by making it clear  we're not withdrawing from Iraq we're  not stopping the fight against Isis and  we're not seeding the territory and the  regional control to Iran that is a good  message for the president to assent but  can I just add something Jason sure I  think it would be worthwhile just  there's all this focus right now on what  this means and the president's rough  week and the press has all been  struggling and focusing on that this is  just a straightforward story of a  president going over to visit the troops  saying hello which is a customary thing  to do and we should be celebrating it  for that in and of itself so mark do you  think we're going to see a lot of  Corrections on the front pages of the  newspapers and talk shows across the  country is that going to happen no  absolutely not they're already picking  apart every word that he said and to  Kim's point the only video and the only  audio we really need to hear is are  those troops who were chanting USA USA  when the president and first lady walked  in there they loved their  commander-in-chief in Donald Trump you  know dr. Gorka wanted that I think the  important messages to the troops is that  we as Americans all of us Americans no  matter your political stripes that we  stand behind the troops it was it's just  a photo-op I mean the criticism is hey  Donald Trump didn't go there and then as  soon as he goes there they say oh it's  just for a photo-op what does this mean  and what is the message that President  Trump is saying to the men and women and  their families who put their lives in  line for our United States military and  for this country Jason it has nothing to  do the photo opportunity it's it was  leaked so now I can discuss it in the  second month of the administration we  had 18 future Green Berets visiting the  eeob the Eisenhower building next to the  White House after their visit to the NSC  I took them to meet the president the  president took time out of his schedule  to meet these young officers each one  was  photographed next to the president at  the resolute desk not because those  photographs can be used in public  because these are our cutting-edge Army  Special Forces guys those photographs  never see the light of day but he wanted  to give something to them to give back  to show them that he's so respects  anyone that wears the cloth of the  Republic or law enforcement I've seen it  again and again and again the first  thing the president does when he gets  off Air Force One when there are no  cameras there at that base he gets off  and he goes down and he shakes the hand  of every police outrider to show his  respect this is a man who loves those  people and it makes such a change after  the Obama is know it does and the  president is on the ground as we speak  at the Ramstein Air Force Base there in  the Germany it's the middle of the night  but he's there visiting with troops you  know those Air Force bases are working  24/7 and the president is there on the  ground as we speak Kim I also want to  talk though about the other big news  that happened today which was the stock  market a thousand point gain which is  not a typical day there has been some  volatility on the market how do you read  into that what what are the swings  attributed to and where should investors  look and where are they going the first  thing is it was good news that the White  House came out today and made clear that  the Fed chief Jerome Powell his job was  secure okay because that was some of the  uncertainty that we were seeing out  there but look I think there comes a  point at which the market just steps  back and maybe that's what we saw today  and realize that despite all the talk  about the uncertainty that is out there  on China and trade deals the shutdown  etc that the fundamentals of the economy  remain really strong and we're seeing  that come in really robust holiday sales  we're going to have GDP GDP come in at a  very strong number this year  unemployment remains low all of these  things that are key indicators of  economic strength and manufacturing in  other areas they really are looking good  and hopefully that's what you're seeing  today is a bit of a correction with  regards to the market and the markets  not an indicator of the economy  obviously but it takes its cue from  economic signals and hopefully this is a  return to a little bit of rationality  about the  future and the prospects for us growth  now Marco one of the things the  president also said while he was in Iraq  is that he plans to visit the southern  border what would you like to see the  president do and how does this play into  the shutdown fight then discussions that  we have going on at almost an hourly  basis right now I want to I want to see  him highlight the great work that  Customs and Border Patrol does every day  even during the shutdown to keep out a  little illegal immigration stop gang  members and drugs from flowing into our  country and show the rest of the world  what we who know the statistics no walls  work and it's easy to demonstrate that  through real-life examples and so I  think the president will highlight that  and it will set the stage for not only  the negotiations with Speaker Pelosi but  it will set the stage for a very strong  State of the Union speech that I can  almost guarantee you will have a very  heavy focus on immigration reform  broad-based immigration reform and  securing our borders yeah when the  president gets an hour or two to address  the nation in that State of the Union  affair and he gets to talk in front of  members of Congress I've been there in  the audience to listen eight times to  Barack Obama try to tell me the way the  world was it was a fascinating thing but  dr. Berkey the president's going down to  the southern border what's the message  you would like to see the president  portray well marks right in addition to  recognizing the incredible work of CBP  and ice and everybody that wears uniform  and protects us at the border there's  one very simple message the wall will be  built and the border is a national  security issue Jason you know as well as  anybody else this isn't about you know  illegals who are turned into a voting  base for the Democrats this is about  ms-13 it's about drug trafficking it's  about women who are raped as they come  across the border mine is being handed  into the hands of coyotes this is a  national security issue and that is how  the president is going to represent it  to all of America whether Chuck Schumer  or Nancy likes it or not  no look I think you're absolutely right  and stay tuned with us later in the show  we're gonna talk some more about that in  depth but thank you very much during  this holiday season for joining  here tonight we do appreciate it

